  "description": "The read succeeds, a real change is detected, and the REWRITE reports DFHRESP(NOTFND): the second arm of UPDATE-USER-SEC-FILE's EVALUATE at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:377-382. The outcome is forced, because a rewrite that follows a successful read-for-update cannot legitimately report NOTFND - it takes a record deleted by another task between the two calls, which no arrangement of seeded rows can arrange.\n\nThe arm issues 'User ID NOT found...' - the same text the read's NOTFND arm issues, from a different paragraph - and moves -1 into USRIDINL, where the rewrite's WHEN OTHER arm moves it to FNAMEL instead. The cursor is therefore what distinguishes the two failures, and it is pinned. Nothing is written: expectedWrites is empty and the ten seeded rows stand unchanged.",
